Package: Loupe2R
Type: Package
Title: Import 10x Genomics Visium '.cloupe' Files into Seurat Objects
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Niel", "Infante", email = "nielinfante@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Extracts count matrices, spatial coordinates, tissue images, UMAP
    embeddings, and cluster labels from 10x Genomics .cloupe files (including
    Visium HD) and imports them into Seurat objects via a Python extraction
    step (reticulate). Requires the Python package 'loupe2py' (not bundled;
    see 'SystemRequirements').
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2R
BugReports: https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2R/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    Seurat (>= 5.0.0),
    SeuratObject,
    methods,
    reticulate,
    png,
    jsonlite,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    arrow,
    digest,
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with the loupe2py package
    (https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2Py), installed separately by the
    user, e.g. via 'pip install git+https://github.com/niel-infante/Loupe2Py.git'
    -- NOT bundled with or distributed by this R package. loupe2py pulls in
    numpy/scipy/Pillow itself and vendors its own copy of the .cloupe binary
    parser, so no further Python-side setup is needed.
